description:
**Skill required:**
Master Data Management - Master Data Management (MDM)


**Designation:**
Sales Prog & Incentive Mgmt Associate


**Qualifications:**
Any Graduation


**Years of Experience:**
1 to 3 years


**About Accenture**
Accenture is a global professional services company with leading capabilities in digital, cloud and security.Combining unmatched experience and specialized skills across more than 40 industries, we offer Strategy and Consulting, Technology and Operations services, and Accenture Song— all powered by the world’s largest network of Advanced Technology and Intelligent Operations centers. Our 784,000 people deliver on the promise of technology and human ingenuity every day, serving clients in more than 120 countries. We embrace the power of change to create value and shared success for our clients, people, shareholders, partners and communities.Visit us at www.accenture.com


**What would you do?**
The Junior Data Management Analyst is responsible for maintaining and securing the accuracy of Master Data in the SAP database, ensuring system integrity and compliance with internal and external procedures. Master Data is a critical information source for SAP systems, supporting most business processes across CLIENT. The role ensures that data is accurate, timely updated, duplicate-free, and managed in a controlled and compliant manner This position also supports users across GBS with Master Data-related issues in systems such as SAP, Blackline, and CRA. The goal is to maintain an error-free, well-governed Master Data environment that ensures smooth operational performance for CLIENT companies.


**What are we looking for?**
University Bachelor’s Degree (Finance, Business, IT, or related field preferred) Additional certifications or SAP training is a plus Bachelor’s degree or diploma holder in a relevant field Basic understanding of SAP systems and database logic Exposure to shared services or multinational working environments is a plus Experience in Master Data creation and maintenance is a plus Strong MS Office skills (Excel, Word, Access, PowerPoint) Good English communication and comprehension skills Analytical thinking, problem-solving, and attention to detail Time management and task prioritization Ability to work under pressure and manage deadlines Effective communication and stakeholder engagement skills


**Roles and Responsibilities:**

* Creation and maintenance of Data objects in accordance with standard procedures of GBS;
* Ensure service levels and targets are consistent with quality and timeliness, and that service is delivered in accordance with agreed TAT.
* Ensuring timeless, accuracy and completeness of all Master Data, identifying and resolving data quality issues;
* Ensure that Data Management processes are in accordance with the internal and external audit requirements;
* Maintaining robust data management policies, procedures and processes, and a robust control environment;
* Ensure a controlled environment in which all reports are accurately and timely rolled out, in line with all global standards;
* Proactively communicate and collaborate with stakeholders to analyse information needs and functional requirements;
* Raise issues to technical team, provide required information, and make active follow-up on open incidents;
* Ensure ad-hoc reports extracted from the system are processed in line with Service Level Agreement (SLA);
* Assist with Monthly / Bi-Annually Cleanse exercises for data objects in scope;
* Deliver trainings to new joiners;
* Ensuring accurate and timely update of TLDs delegated by Data Management (Task Level Descriptions) and the knowledge transfer within the DM team.

The ideal candidate is a motivated, well-organized individual who has a deep understanding of prospecting and developing strong relationships with customers.

Responsibilities：

1. Responsible for sales and market expansion in the area under its jurisdiction;

2. Establish and maintain relationships with agents (dealers);

3. Responsible for planning and implementing the company's international brand image;

4. Achieving international sales targets and negotiating with foreign customers;

5. Planning and implementation of international industry exhibitions;

6. Communication and coordination with foreign clients or relevant hospitals;

7. Provide product training and after-sales service training to foreign customers.

Job requirements:

1. Bachelor's degree in Medicine, Biomedical Engineering, Marketing, International Economics and Trade, or Science and Engineering;

2. More than 3 years of sales experience in the medical device industry, with priority given to imaging products.

3. Strong resilience, strong business development and learning abilities.

Responsibilities：




 1\. Responsible for the energy storage project development in the India, actively expanding overseas markets;




 2\. Conduct research on market product planning requirements, share the information with




 relevant support departments, develop solutions, and assist in designing products suitable for the market;




 3\. Develop global partnerships and establish a robust upstream and downstream business ecosystem in BESS industry, including developing partnerships with local developers, consultants, grid




 companies and financial facilities.




 4\. Building the company's brand and competitiveness;










 Job Requirements:




 1\. Bachelor's degree or above, with a major in battery, engineering, or electrical power preferred;




 Priority will be given to candidates with over 2\-3 years of experience in market development for




 photovoltaic inverters, photovoltaic modules, and energy storage;




 2\.Candidates familiar with Asia Pacific cultures and with overseas study, living, or work experience will be preferred;




 3\. Fluent in English.
